<title>HONG KONG: British PM Blair arrives for HK handover ceremony.</title>
<headline>British PM Blair arrives for HK handover ceremony.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister Tony Blair on Monday flew into Hong Kong to attend the ceremony marking the handover of the colony to China after 156 years of British rule.</p>
<p>Blair will spend just 11 hours in the territory, during which he will hold talks with Chinese President Jiang Zemin.</p>
</text>
